    url: /en/calculators/
  - name: Trip Cost After Points Calculator
    url: /en/calculators/trip-cost-after-points/
faqItems:
  - question: Why is my out-of-pocket cost not zero after using points?
    answer: Airline loyalty programs only cover the base airfare. Government taxes, airport departure fees, customs inspections, and airline-imposed carrier surcharges (YQ/YR) must still be paid in cash. For long-haul flights, these cash taxes can range from $50 to several hundred dollars.
  - question: Do I have to pay resort or destination fees on award hotel stays?
    answer: It depends on the loyalty program. World of Hyatt and Hilton Honors waive resort/destination fees completely on award stays. Marriott Bonvoy and IHG One Rewards generally still charge daily resort/destination fees at the front desk even on award bookings.
  - question: When is it better to pay cash instead of using points?
    answer: Paying cash is recommended when mandatory award taxes are excessive, when your realized CPP is below the conservative threshold for that program (e.g. below 1.2¢ for airlines or 0.6¢ for Marriott), or when cash airfares/hotel rates are extraordinarily cheap and earn significant redeemable and elite status miles.
  - question: Is my budget or points balance data sent to any server?
    answer: No. All calculations and budget data run 100% locally in your browser (clientside). We do not collect, store, or transmit your financial information or personal travel itineraries.
