  <h2>Frequently Asked Questions (FAQ)</h2>
  <details class="faq-item">
    <summary><strong>Why is my out-of-pocket cost not zero after using points?</strong></summary>
    <p>Airline loyalty programs only cover the base airfare. Government taxes, airport departure fees, customs inspections, and airline-imposed carrier surcharges (YQ/YR) must still be paid in cash. For long-haul flights, these cash taxes can range from $50 to several hundred dollars.</p>
  </details>
  <details class="faq-item">
    <summary><strong>Do I have to pay resort or destination fees on award hotel stays?</strong></summary>
    <p>It depends on the loyalty program. World of Hyatt and Hilton Honors waive resort/destination fees completely on award stays. Marriott Bonvoy and IHG One Rewards generally still charge daily resort/destination fees at the front desk even on award bookings.</p>
  </details>
  <details class="faq-item">
    <summary><strong>When is it better to pay cash instead of using points?</strong></summary>
    <p>Paying cash is recommended when mandatory award taxes are excessive, when your realized CPP is below the conservative threshold for that program (e.g. below 1.2¢ for airlines or 0.6¢ for Marriott), or when cash airfares/hotel rates are extraordinarily cheap and earn significant redeemable and elite status miles.</p>
  </details>
  <details class="faq-item">
    <summary><strong>Is my budget or points balance data sent to any server?</strong></summary>
    <p>No. All calculations and budget data run 100% locally in your browser (clientside). We do not collect, store, or transmit your financial information or personal travel itineraries.</p>
  </details>

  <h2>Disclaimer & Editorial Integrity</h2>
  <p class="disclaimer">
    Calculations and recommendations provided by this tool are for budgeting and educational purposes only and do not constitute financial or investment advice. Award space availability, cash rates, and transfer ratios are subject to dynamic real-time changes by loyalty programs.<br>
